    "sha": "733ea76c719a86e60c2fd9983fe9b1c7d2d8dcf4",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDczM2VhNzZjNzE5YTg2ZTYwYzJmZDk5ODNmZTliMWM3ZDJkOGRjZjQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-12T08:09:37Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-12T08:09:37Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui): original SVG operation icons and the SVG-to-PNG icon pipeline\n\nEvery OpType now wears its own glyph: 41 original SVG masters under\nassets/ui/svg/ (Tabler's conventions - 24-unit grid, 2-unit stroke,\nround caps and joins; nothing from HSMWorks, Fusion or SolidCraft),\nrasterised to the 32 px PNGs the UI loads by the new `cargo xtask icons`\n(resvg =0.45.1, xtask-only; --check compares the committed PNGs with\nfresh renders, --sheet draws a 16 px contact sheet on dark and light).\n\nicons.rs becomes one table (enum, ALL, bytes, keys from a macro); the\nop-kind mapping moves out of panes.rs into op_icons.rs and drops the old\nreuse law. The 18 PNGs no longer used (13 earlier originals, 5 Tabler\nstand-ins) are deleted. Pinned by xtask's\ncommitted_icon_pngs_match_their_svg_masters and the lint tests, and the\nstructural test every_op_kind_has_its_own_svg_mastered_icon.\n\nxtask/ is a process file: PROCESS_VERSION 16 -> 17.\nDecision: docs/decisions/661-icon-set.md.\n\nRefs #661\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
